The files in this directory (firmware/src/wind/ and its shim/) are FM-1 Windsynth's instrument: the
wind voice, wind control, the mod matrix, the effects and the parameters that tie them together.

This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0. If a copy of
the MPL was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
The full text is in LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt at the top of this repository.

They are free to use in other firmware, closed or open, on the MPL's terms: these files, and your
changes to them, stay under the MPL, and if you ship them in an executable you make their source
available and tell recipients how to get it (MPL-2.0 sections 3.1 and 3.2). In this firmware they are combined with GPL-3.0-only code, and the firmware as a
whole is distributed under GPL-3.0-only (MPL-2.0 section 3.3).

What these files depend on:
- wind_math.h includes ../dsp/fastmath.h, which is FoMni's / X0X's, GPL-3.0-only, and not covered by this
  licence. Build with -DWIND_MATH_LIBM to use the C library's maths instead (it sounds the same,
  but is not sample-identical to this firmware).
- wind_voice.cc wraps Plaits and stmlib (Mutable Instruments, Emilie Gillet), MIT, vendored in
  firmware/third_party/mutable/, and its filter and noise loudness are adapted from Plaits: those
  portions keep Plaits' MIT copyright and notice (firmware/third_party/mutable/LICENSE).
